==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*kezdō}}, further derivation disputed.

* Perhaps it is from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*ḱyesdʰ-||to drive away; to go away}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|सेधति||to drive, chase away}} and {{cog|ae|𐬯𐬌𐬌𐬀𐬰𐬛𐬀𐬝|t=will chase away}}, from {{cog|iir-pro|*ćyazd-}}, {{m|iir-pro|*ćižd-}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|pages=103-104|head=cēdō, -ere}}</ref>
* Others refer the Proto-Italic verb as from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*ḱye}}, adverb from {{m|ine-pro|*ḱe||here}}, + {{m|ine-pro|*sed-||to sit}}. Compare the semantics of {{cog|en|set out}} and Ancient Greek {{m|grc|ὁδός}}.
* Other derive the ending from {{m|la|-dō|t=put}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|cēdō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|cēdō|cess|cess}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[go]], [[move]], [[proceed]], [[go along]], [[move]] along
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Pseudolus|4|1|44|thru=45|quote=SIMŌ. Illīcine est? PSEUDOLUS. Illīc est. SIMŌ. Mala merx est, Pseudole. Illūc sīs vidē,<br>ut trānsvorsus, nōn prōvorsus '''cēdit''', quasi cancer solet.|trans=SIMO. Is he there? PSEUDOLUS. There he is. SIMO. He's a bad piece, Pseudolus. Look at that,<br>how he '''goes''' sideways, not forwards, as a crab does.}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[result]], [[turn out]], [[happen]], [[yield]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[withdraw]], [[depart]], [[retire]], go away from, [[yield]]
## {{lb|la|intransitive|military}} to withdraw, [[fall back]], [[give up]] one's post, [[yield]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[disappear]], [[pass away]], [[vanish]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive|of time}} to [[pass]], [[elapse]] {{gl|in the 3rd person, with time as subject}}
#: {{syn|la|intercēdō|abeō|lābor|praetereō}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive|with dative}} to [[cede]], [[give in]] or [[yield]] (to), [[step aside]] (for), [[give way]] (to)
#* [[w:Virgil|Vergilius]], [[w:Aeneid|Aeneis]], Book VI, line 95
#*: Tū nē '''cēde''' malīs, sed contrā audentior ītō
#*:: '''Give in''' not to evils, but go against them more daring.
#* Motto of Wyoming
#*: '''Cēdant''' arma togae.
#*:: Let the arms '''concede''' to the toga (Let war yield to diplomacy)
## {{lb|la|intransitive}} to be [[inferior]] to, yield to in rank
##* {{Q|la|[[w:Titus Livius|Titus Livius]]|[[w:Ab Urbe Condita Libri|Ab Urbe Condita]]|I, 2|quote=Nec deinde Aborigines Troianis studio ac fide erga regem [[w:Aeneas|Aeneam]] '''cessere'''|t=From that time on, the Aborigines were not '''inferior to''' the Trojans in the loyalty towards [[w:Aeneas|Aeneas]]}}
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[concede]], give up, [[allow]], [[permit]] something to someone, [[grant]], [[surrender]], [[yield]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive|with dative or in +acc.}} to [[fall]] (to) (as a possession); [[accrue]] or [[come]] (to)
# {{lb|la|intransitive|with in +acc.}} to [[become]], [[turn into]], be or become the [[equivalent]] of

