===Etymology 2===
Through iambic shortening from the {{inh|la|itc-pro|-}} imperative {{m|itc-pro|*kedō|*ke-dō}}, plural {{m|itc-pro|*kedate|*ke-date}}. This is composed of  {{inh|la|ine-pro|*ḱe||here}} (seen also in {{m|la|ecce|ec-ce}}, {{m|la|hic|hi-c}}, {{m|la|illic|illi-c}} etc.) + the imperative of {{m|la|dō||give}} (which was originally {{m|la||*dō}}, but changed later to {{m|la|dā}} by analogy with first-conjugation verbs). Equivalent to {{confix|la|ce|dō}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|cedo}}

====Verb====
{{head|la|verb|second person imperative||plural|cette}}

# {{lb|la|of objects}} hand (it) over!; give (it)!; gimme!
#: {{uxi|la|'''cedo''' manum!|Give me your hand!}}
# {{lb|la|of objects|especially evidence or exhibits at a trial}} produce (it)!; show (it) to us!
# {{lb|la|of people}} bring (him)!, bring (him) in!, produce (him)!
# tell me!; describe (it) to me!, explain (it) to me!
#* {{Q|la|Apuleius|Metamorphoses|1|8|quote="Ōrō tē" inquam "aulaeum tragicum dīmovētō et sīparium scaenicum complicātō et '''cedo''' verbīs commūnibus."|t=I said, "I beg you, please remove the tragic drapery and fold the scene's curtain, and '''explain it to me''' using common words.}}
# {{lb|la|followed by a conditional clause with consequent}} tell me! come now! hear me out!
# {{lb|la|followed by a conditional clause without a consequent}} what if?, suppose?
# {{lb|la|with impersonal or subjunctive}} [[come now]]!

=====Conjugation=====
Imperative only:
* Second person singular: {{m|la||cedo}}
* Second person plural: {{m|la|cette}}

